The `@api_view` decorator defaults to accepting only `GET` methods. By default, any other method, including `POST`, will respond with a "405 Method Not Allowed" error.

To allow `POST` requests, you must explicitly specify the allowed methods in the decorator. Update your view as follows:

```python
@api_view(['GET', 'POST'])
def create_thing(request):
    thing = Thing.objects.create(**request.data)
    return Response(ThingSerializer(thing).data, status=201)
```

The reason your class-based views work without this configuration is that they use the `APIView` class, which operates differently than the function-based `@api_view` decorator.

